# The version of the image and of the GitHub release.
#
# Write MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH with no "v" at the start. A suffix after a hyphen,
# for example 1.1.0-beta or 1.1.0-beta.2, is published as a pre-release.
# Any other value stops the build and prints an error.
#
# Only a new MAJOR.MINOR creates a release:
#
#   breaks an existing setup   1.4.2 -> 2.0.0   release
#   new feature                1.4.2 -> 1.5.0   release
#   fix only                   1.4.2 -> 1.4.3   no release, appended to the v1.4 release notes
#
# Every merge to main publishes the image as `latest`, `sha-<short>` and the
# exact version, so a patch still reaches the container without a release.
#
# Change this file in the same PR as the work it releases.

1.0.1-beta
